    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0541" n="1275" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1275"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mavroyeni Bey.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August 22,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 31.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your two notes of the 17th and 18th instant, special Nos. 40 and 41,
                    reporting the substance of a telegram which you have received from, the Sublime
                    Porte in regard to the recent occurrences at Tarsus, of which mention has been
                    made in the press. Upon calling the attention of the United States minister at
                    Constantinople to the published reports, Mr. Terrell answered that he had
                    already obtained from the Imperial Government, on the 7th instant, a promise to
                    investigate the incident, and I presume that I shall in due course receive from
                    the legation the report of which your notes communicate to me the substance.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
